# `a b a b` against `a b`: two minimal answers exist and diff picks one. The
# tool deletes the *later* pair, which is what a greedy forward pass does --
# it takes the longest snake it can reach first, so the deletion lands after
# it. This case exists to pin the tie-breaking rather than the distance.
args:
first:
a
b
a
b
input:
a
b
